# Design reference

Before CSS/UI polish, consult:

- `.cursor/rules/ui-styling.mdc` — components, layout, elements (always on)
- `detailing-app/design-references/` — ScreenDesigns replay frames
- `detailing-app/design-references/MOTION_SPEC.md` — archetypes + animation spec template
- `.cursor/rules/design-motion.mdc` — always-on motion reference (archetypes, frame workflow)
- `detailing-app/design-references/STYLE_PLAN.md` — phased polish plan (read before implementing)
- `detailing-app/design-references/ONBOARDING_EXPERIENCE_CHEATSHEET.md` — onboarding, trial, paywall psychology
- `detailing-app/docs/ui-css-audit.md` — pattern owners; extend, don't duplicate
- `detailing-app/src/app/tokens.css` — surfaces, shadows, motion tokens

## North star: Invoice Fly

Match **depth + motion**, not just colors. Reference frames live in
`design-references/invoice-fly/` (218 webp replay captures).

## When improving a screen

1. Find closest replay frames in `design-references/invoice-fly/`
2. Note motion type: enter, press, success, progress, empty state
3. Check `STYLE_PLAN.md` for phase/priority before coding
4. Extend existing CSS owners from `ui-css-audit.md` — no one-off animation files per page
5. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`

## Adding new ScreenDesigns exports

1. Create `design-references/{app-slug}/`
2. Add a README with screen names and frame ID ranges
3. Update `design-references/README.md` index

## Do not

- Change tokens or animations unless explicitly asked
- Duplicate card/sheet/header rules outside their pattern owners
